===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|tewtéh₂}}
1580, from {{der|en|la|Teutonicus}}, from {{m|la|Teutonēs}}, {{m|la|Teutonī|t=the Teutons|pos=name of a {{der|en|gem|-}} tribe that inhabited coastal Germany and devastated Gaul between 113–101 B.C.}}, equivalent to {{af|en|Teuton|-ic}}.<ref>[http://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/text?doc=Perseus:text:1999.04.0059:entry=teutoni Teutŏni], in Charlton T. Lewis and Charles Short (1879) A Latin Dictionary, Oxford: Clarendon Press</ref>

